import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — conv+BN weight fold: the synthesis attempt, measured","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/conv-bn-fold-synth.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/conv-bn-fold-synth.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/conv-bn-fold-synth.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-conv-bn-weight-fold-the-synthesis-attempt-measured" tabindex="-1">Retro — conv+BN weight fold: the synthesis attempt, measured <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-conv-bn-weight-fold-the-synthesis-attempt-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — conv+BN weight fold: the synthesis attempt, measured”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-10-18. <strong>Follows</strong>: <code>leaf-compose-seam.md</code> (&quot;What stays open&quot;: try <code>synthesize_rules</code>/<code>dspec_synth</code> on a real conv→batch_norm seed rather than hand-writing the fold). <strong>Probe</strong>: <code>lab/probes/conv_bn_fold_synth_probe.py</code> — gate-by-gate, reproducible.</p><p><strong>Verdict</strong>: <code>synthesize_rules</code> <strong>refuses structurally</strong> — the fold&#39;s RHS <code>conv2d(x, W′, b′)</code> is unreachable by composition; <code>dspec_synth</code><strong>mints</strong> the fold&#39;s derive exprs in stages. The named blockers are below; none is the <code>$leaf:</code> seam itself (that works — the emitted composites prove it).</p><h2 id="the-seed" tabindex="-1">The seed <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-seed" aria-label="Permalink to “The seed”">​</a></h2><p>Real export through <code>TorchSource</code>, eval mode, perturbed running stats:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>(batch_norm (conv2d x, p_conv_weight, p_conv_bias,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>              stride=(1, 1), padding=(1, 1)),</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>            p_bn_weight, p_bn_bias, b_bn_running_mean,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>            b_bn_running_var,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>            training=False, momentum=0.1, eps=1e-05,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>            cudnn_enabled=False)</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="gate-a-—-bank-census-conv2d-is-absent-from-the-law-space" tabindex="-1">Gate A — bank census: <code>conv2d</code> is absent from the law space <a class="header-anchor" href="#gate-a-—-bank-census-conv2d-is-absent-from-the-law-space" aria-label="Permalink to “Gate A — bank census: conv2d is absent from the law space”">​</a></h2><p>Across all 86 rules (<code>ALL_RULES</code> 83 + <code>BATCH_NORM_RULES</code> 3): <strong>zero</strong> rules name <code>conv2d</code> in their lhs, <strong>zero</strong> in their rhs; <code>batch_norm</code> appears only in the three expand lhses. Every composite <code>synthesize_rules</code> can emit has rhs <code>r1.rhs</code> with <code>r2.rhs</code> spliced inside — the rhs head set is closed under the parents&#39; heads. A <code>conv2d</code>-headed rhs is therefore <em>structurally unreachable</em> regardless of composition depth: not a depth problem, not a seam problem — a <strong>corpus gap</strong>. The missing piece is an anchor: one <code>conv2d</code>-headed law. The authored precedent is <code>linear_channel_scale</code> (opt-in) — the conv twin <code>conv_channel_scale</code> (<code>mul(conv2d(x,W,b), ŝ) ↔ conv2d(x, mul(W,ŝ′), mul(b,s))</code>) is what the corpus lacks; alternatively an anchored mint path — antiunify over a measured (seed, folded) pair — the ADR-0008 bridge direction.</p><h2 id="gate-b-—-synthesize-rules-on-the-real-seed" tabindex="-1">Gate B — <code>synthesize_rules</code> on the real seed <a class="header-anchor" href="#gate-b-—-synthesize-rules-on-the-real-seed" aria-label="Permalink to “Gate B — synthesize_rules on the real seed”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>bank</th><th>numeric_check</th><th>emitted</th><th>lhs has <code>conv2d</code></th><th>rhs headed <code>conv2d</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>DEFAULT+BN (74)</td><td>False</td><td>5</td><td>1 (<code>syn_batch_norm_expand__sub_to_add_0</code>)</td><td><strong>0</strong></td></tr><tr><td>DEFAULT+BN</td><td>True</td><td>4</td><td>0</td><td><strong>0</strong></td></tr><tr><td>ALL+BN (86)</td><td>False</td><td>32</td><td>6</td><td><strong>0</strong></td></tr><tr><td>ALL+BN</td><td>True</td><td>26</td><td>1</td><td><strong>0</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The seed-guided path <em>does</em> produce the fold&#39;s lhs — leaf-generalization over the LCA region mints <code>batch_norm(conv2d(…))</code> patterns. Inside the expanded term only <code>mul_reshape_inert_l</code> and <code>sub_to_add</code> match under DEFAULT (comm/assoc plumbing is opt-in, not in DEFAULT); under ALL+BN the comm/assoc variants compose too. All rhs heads stay <code>add</code>/<code>mul</code> — the spelled subgraph.</p><h2 id="gate-b2-—-numeric-check-drop-is-a-nan-env-artifact" tabindex="-1">Gate B2 — <code>numeric_check</code> drop is a NaN-env artifact <a class="header-anchor" href="#gate-b2-—-numeric-check-drop-is-a-nan-env-artifact" aria-label="Permalink to “Gate B2 — numeric_check drop is a NaN-env artifact”">​</a></h2><p><code>numeric_check=True</code> drops <code>syn_batch_norm_expand__sub_to_add_0</code>: <code>_tensor_env</code> draws <code>randn</code> envs, so <code>rv &lt; 0</code> makes <strong>both</strong> sides evaluate <code>rsqrt</code> of a negative → <code>allclose(nan, nan) = False</code>. Not an unsound rewrite — a witness-env precondition (<code>var ≥ 0</code>) that shape guards cannot express. Noted so the next sweep doesn&#39;t misread it.</p><h2 id="gates-c-d-—-dspec-synth-mints-the-fold-s-derives-in-stages" tabindex="-1">Gates C/D — <code>dspec_synth</code> mints the fold&#39;s derives <em>in stages</em> <a class="header-anchor" href="#gates-c-d-—-dspec-synth-mints-the-fold-s-derives-in-stages" aria-label="Permalink to “Gates C/D — dspec_synth mints the fold&#39;s derives in stages”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>target</th><th>tier</th><th>result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>scale = γ/√(σ²+ε)</code></td><td>attr scalars</td><td><strong>depth 3</strong>: <code>fdiv(float(float γ), sqrt(add(ε, σ²)))</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>b′ = (b−μ)·scale+β</code></td><td>attr scalars</td><td><strong>depth 3</strong>: <code>add(β, mul(scale, sub(b, μ)))</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>W′ = W·scale</code></td><td>attr scalars</td><td><strong>depth 2</strong> (given <code>scale</code>): <code>mul(attr W, attr scale)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>W′</code> one-shot <code>tval</code></td><td>tensors</td><td><strong>refuse</strong> — depth ≥4 AND <code>(C,)×(C,i,k,k)</code> broadcast decline</td></tr><tr><td><code>W′</code> staged <code>tval</code></td><td>tensors</td><td><strong>depth 2</strong>: <code>mul(tval W, tval s)</code> — needs pushed channel-broadcast <code>mul</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>b′</code> staged <code>tval</code></td><td>tensors</td><td>budget-truncated (level-3 product ≈ 26 G pairs; 14 M checked in 60 s)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>So the fold&#39;s <code>dspec</code> content is mintable; the composition gap is the anchor above. Two <em>sub-gaps</em> named for the tensor tier: (a) the one-shot tree is depth ≥4 — a <strong>staged fit</strong> (mint <code>scale</code> first, then <code>W′</code>/<code>b′</code> over it) is required, which today&#39;s single-shot <code>synth_dspec</code> API doesn&#39;t do; (b) full-tensor <code>W′</code> needs either a <strong>pushed channel-broadcast <code>mul</code></strong> convention (adapter-owned typing — demonstrated in the probe) or <code>tapp</code>/reshape in the enumeration bank (<code>tapp</code> evaluates; it is not enumerated).</p><h2 id="lab-bug-fixed-en-route" tabindex="-1">Lab bug fixed en route <a class="header-anchor" href="#lab-bug-fixed-en-route" aria-label="Permalink to “Lab bug fixed en route”">​</a></h2><p><code>lab/audit/dspec_audit.py::bounded_synth</code> predated the ADR-0012 <code>_vkey</code> boxing: <code>values = {v for _b, v in samples}</code> crashed <code>TypeError: unhashable type: &#39;numpy.ndarray&#39;</code> on tensor-valued samples, and its sig/expected equality compared raw arrays (<code>v != expected[i]</code> → ambiguous truthiness). Ported <code>synth_dspec</code>&#39;s split — <code>_vkey</code> fingerprints for the constant check and <code>_box</code> for signature equality; ints-only literal seeds unchanged.</p><h2 id="what-stays-open-named-ordered" tabindex="-1">What stays open (named, ordered) <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open-named-ordered" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open (named, ordered)”">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>The anchor</strong> — a <code>conv2d</code>-headed law (channel-scale absorb) or an anchored mint path (<code>antiunify</code>/<code>atom_synth_loop</code> over a measured seed↔folded pair). Until one exists, composition has no <code>conv2d</code> rhs material. Once it does, <code>batch_norm_expand</code> + the spelled reassociation + the absorb compose — the <code>$leaf:</code> seam carries the minted weights.</li><li><strong>Staged dspec fitting</strong> — the fold&#39;s derive mints only when <code>scale</code> is a bound leaf: a <code>synth_dspec</code> that threads a previously-minted derive as a leaf.</li><li><strong><code>tapp</code>/reshape or broadcast-mul in the enumeration bank</strong> — the <code>(C,)×(C,i,k,…)</code> broadcast declines under vanilla numpy <code>mul</code>.</li><li><code>BATCH_NORM_RULES</code> <code>DEFAULT</code> admission — the guarded sweep (item 2 of this work order).</li></ol>`,20)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};